//? Title: Offline LCA: actual finish events, unions and query answers
//? Subtitle: Actual canonical histories, retained original fixtures and explicit controls
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Knowing all ancestor queries in advance lets one depth-first traversal answer
them with union-find. The original eight-node tree retains its seven query
types, and actual finish/union events explain the representative ancestor
invariant.
)

\toc

> Mechanism and mathematical scope

Initialize singleton disjoint sets and ancestor[representative]=node. Finish
every child subtree, merge it with its parent by rank and reset the merged
representative ancestor to that parent. Mark u black when its subtree is
complete. For a query(u,v) with v already black, answer ancestor[find(v)]. Path
compression/rank give near-linear O((n+q)*alpha(n)) producing work, plus the
disclosed complete-tree validation. Explicit frames avoid recursion. Self
queries occur at both endpoint lists and may write the same answer twice.

> A tiny actual producing history

The table and native concept diagram read the same producing execution. Every
block below is a complete editable C++ program.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/tarjan_lca_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto r = a::tarjan_lca_trace(3, 0, {{0, 1}, {0, 2}}, {{1, 2}, {1, 1}});
    std::print("| actual action | node | other | query index | representative | representative ancestor " "|\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (const auto &s : r.steps)
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", s.action, s.vertex,
                   s.other, s.query, s.representative, s.ancestor);
    g::Diagram concept_diagram(48, 1100);
    concept_diagram.node("n0", {0, 0}, "Actual root0 with children1,2");
    concept_diagram.node("n1", {5, 0},
                         std::format("{} actual child-to-parent unions",
                                     r.unions));
    concept_diagram.node("n2", {10, 0},
                         std::format("Actual query answers {}", r.lca));
    concept_diagram.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    concept_diagram.save_svg("build/tarjan_lca_tiny.svg");
}
```
