> API and interpretation

Nonempty tree geometry, every query ID, connectivity and absence of
cycles/duplicate edges are validated before producing DFS. The old
edge-count-only validator could loop on cyclic input; this now fails explicitly.
Captured events use already computed representatives without adding find calls.
The representative at a black event is tracked through actual unions, which
matters when rank chooses a child representative.

Reusable producers, fixtures and histories live in the canonical C++ library.
Captured records own their values and do not come from a separate report replay.
Selected counters and record/scalar policies are specified at their API
boundaries; they are not peak-byte or wall-time budgets. Synthetic structural
inputs are controlled fixtures for these mechanisms.

> References

- [Tarjan, Applications of Path Compression on Balanced Trees, JACM26 (1979),690-715|https://doi.org/10.1145/322154.322161]

